From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: draw the external taskbar ReBar's grippers and unused tail

Purpose: show Luna's taskbar grippers and background in the native ReBar.
XP behavior: the gripper has the theme's cross-axis thickness at the band
header's origin over its full long axis, and the theme's margins and tiling
repeat the grip; the region behind the task band's child that it leaves
unused shows the taskbar background.
Wine before: the native ReBar closed its generic theme on SetWindowTheme and
painted a classic gripper.
Change: keep its window procedure, input, layout and dragging; after it
paints, overlay the hidden-title band headers with the themed parent
background and the Taskbar::Rebar gripper at RB_GETRECT and RB_GETBANDINFOW
geometry, and paint the unused tail with the parent background. Print DC
state and clipping are kept, and destruction during the native paint is
handled.
Evidence: tests/rebar-theme.c, tests/rebar-gripper.c, tests/rebar-tail.c
compare with direct theme drawing, translated print DCs, native input and
disabling the override.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL and the Taskbar theme.
Old patches: 0021, 0029, 0038.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/Makefile.in  |   1 +
 dlls/uxtheme/rebar.c      | 155 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/uxtheme/system.c     |   1 +
 dlls/uxtheme/uxthemedll.h |   1 +
 4 files changed, 158 insertions(+)

